Runtime-verified with g++ and clang++ (-std=c++20): the assertion
holds natively (primary selected, value=false).  CBMC selects the
partial specialization instead (no two-phase lookup) and the
assertion FAILS.  Fix requires point-of-declaration awareness in the
resolver for dependent unqualified calls inside specialization
patterns, or a targeted ordering check at the spec-matching site.
Round-28 fix (2026-08-09): ordinary-lookup candidates declared later
in the same file than the dependent use are filtered in SFINAE
contexts (approximating the definition-point rule; ADL still adds
instantiation-point candidates per [temp.point]).
